<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-archaeopteris-hibernica-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Archaeopteris hibernica Famennian epidermal Turing wavelength (31 µm, 370 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 88.5/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 closes the three Pass 1 gaps. Equal-diffusion amplitude ratio is 0.246 after t=140 (was 0.669 at t=24). The seeded pattern is 31.0 µm and the unseeded pattern at the same gamma is 26.57 µm, a finite-amplitude shift of 4.43 µm, now printed on the comparison figure and stored in metrics.json. Dispersion Pearson r = 0.9865, RMSE = 0.0375. Specimen orientation KS = 0.25, radial-spectrum Pearson r = 0.994, radial RMSE = 0.257. GIF CV similarity remains 96.0 at 630x720, 12 frames. gamma sweep stays monotone from 62 µm down to 15.5 µm analytical. Overall 88.5/100 (faithfulness 88.3, reproducibility 88.9); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc; environment: python 3.12, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 90, Morphological realism / specimen match 86, Parameter expressivity 88, Morphometric validation 90, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 86, Reproducibility package 90. Output judged: docs/media/archaeopteris_hibernica_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-archaeopteris-hibernica-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc, image/png, 473788 B, 1512×1008 px, artifact_sha256 75313c23bb6bc7bf8b0b66f01aebf299fc058dea9c8878642efc4ea37fa104a8 (sha256 75313c23bb6bc7bf8b0b66f01aebf299fc058dea9c8878642efc4ea37fa104a8), spec_fingerprint a4e175a99a098be3c6247b8689ef9fb8b86a807901aee40d5798aca5032374bc. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: a4e175a99a098be3c6247b8689ef9fb8b86a807901aee40d5798aca5032374bc; artifact_sha256: 75313c23bb6bc7bf8b0b66f01aebf299fc058dea9c8878642efc4ea37fa104a8; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/archaeopteris_hibernica_turing_wavelength_s0/Archaeopteris_hibernica_NMNH.jpg=20c480a93bc91bf3..., datasets/archaeopteris_hibernica_turing_wavelength_s0/archaeopteris_hibernica_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=655a409a6f13bf84..., datasets/archaeopteris_hibernica_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=4912199010e7d045...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-archaeopteris-hibernica-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Meyer-Berthaud, Scheckler and Wendt (1999) establish a planated megaphyll and modern tree habit for Archaeopteris by the Famennian. | Turing (1952) gives a diffusion-driven instability at a critical wavenumber. | Schnakenberg (1979) supplies the two-species kinetics used here. | Boyce and Knoll (2002) treat planation as the step that makes a laminate leaf.; reconstructed_in_script: gamma = 0.6636 so that argmax sigma(k) = 2*pi/31 per micrometre on this Jacobian. | Thickness scaling lambda(h) = 31*(h/12.4)^0.62 gives 66 µm (Tetraxylopteris, 385 Ma) and 21 µm (Elkinsia, 365 Ma). | The GIF multiplies the museum frond by a resized activator veil. The photograph does not resolve 31 µm cells. | The 4.43 µm seeded-versus-unseeded shift is a finite-amplitude effect on the 186 µm grid, not a second biological wavelength.; transfer_boundary: An animal pigment Turing pattern is being used as the kinetics for a fossil epidermis whose original chemistry is not preserved.; does_not_claim: That 31 µm was measured on the Smithsonian slab or in the 1999 Nature paper. | That the predecessor and successor wavelengths are direct fossil measurements. | That nanopublications were signed. No ~/.nanopub/profile.yml is present, so sign_morphoeval.py cannot run.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:hasScore 8.85e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-archaeopteris-hibernica-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Archaeopteris hibernica Famennian epidermal Turing wavelength (31 µm, 370 Ma) — Parameter expressivity: 88/100" ;
